}
```

Types and signatures, in existing modules:

```rust
// domain/models/entity_details.rs
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct CalendarYear(i32);

impl CalendarYear {
    pub fn containing(at: DateTime<Utc>) -> Self; // at.year()
    pub fn value(self) -> i32;
    pub fn contains(self, at: DateTime<Utc>) -> bool; // at.year() == self.0
}

pub struct DeclaredGbpTotals {
    pub calendar_year: CalendarYear,
    pub current_year: DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal,
    // Existing current_term_start, current_term, historical unchanged.
}

// domain/services/entity_details.rs
fn summarize_member(history: MemberHistory, year: CalendarYear) -> MemberDetails;
```

Add a third `PeriodAggregate` to the existing traversal. Observe each declaration when its `registered_at` exists and `year.contains(date)`. This shares every currency, precision, completeness, category and count rule with existing periods. Year equality implements the UTC half-open calendar-year interval without constructing boundaries or introducing overflow at the largest supported year.

Wire and consumer changes:

- `inbound/http/handlers/entity_details.rs`: add mandatory numeric `calendar_year` using `CalendarYear::value()` and mandatory `current_year` through existing period conversion.
- `frontend/src/lib/entity-details.ts`: add `calendarYear: number` and `currentYear: DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal`.
- `frontend/src/lib/server/entity-details.ts`: parse the year as an integer and the period through `declaredPeriod`; reject missing fields.
- Existing MemberIdentity caller: append the year metric to the same metrics array, using existing formatting. Use “No declarations recorded” when `declarationCount === 0`; never infer emptiness from null or zero amounts.
- Extend existing service, serialization, parser and view fixtures/tests. Include Dec 31/Jan 1 UTC transitions, following-year exclusion, undated records, unknown categories, missing GBP, foreign currencies, exact decimals and zero.

Alternative: represent the period as `RegistrationRange { start, end }`. That generalizes to arbitrary reporting intervals but exposes two correlated timestamps plus a separate display year. For this single calendar-year feature, `CalendarYear` gives the smaller interface and owns inclusion and labeling together. No repository or database changes are needed.

Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER
Task name: /root
Sender: /root/design_sol
Payload:
Caller usage:

```rust
// Service boundary captures time once.
let as_of = Utc::now();
history.map(|history| summarize_member(history, as_of))

// Pure summary; tests supply an explicit timestamp.
summarize_member(history, utc("2026-10-23T12:00:00Z"))
```

```svelte
{
  label: `Declared amounts in ${dateLabelYear(summary.declaredTotals.calendarYearStart)}`,
  total: summary.declaredTotals.calendarYear,
}
```

Append this to the existing metric collection; retain `Metric` properties and change empty metric text to `"No declarations recorded"`.

Types and signatures:

```rust
/// UTC interval [January 1, January 1 of following year).
/// Private boundaries; construction establishes ordering and calendar alignment.
struct CalendarYearPeriod {
    start: DateTime<Utc>,
    end: DateTime<Utc>,
}

impl CalendarYearPeriod {
    fn containing(as_of: DateTime<Utc>) -> Self;
    fn includes(&self, registered_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>) -> bool;
}

fn summarize_member(
    history: MemberHistory,
    as_of: DateTime<Utc>,
) -> MemberDetails;
```

Extend `DeclaredGbpTotals` with:

```rust
pub calendar_year_start: DateTime<Utc>,
pub calendar_year: DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal,
```

Inside the existing declaration loop, observe each declaration into a third `PeriodAggregate` when its timestamp is in the calendar interval. Reuse `gbp_total()` unchanged.

Files:

- `domain/services/entity_details.rs`: calendar interval, timestamp parameter, aggregate.
- `domain/models/entity_details.rs`: mandatory calendar fields.
- `inbound/http/handlers/entity_details.rs`: serialize those fields with existing decimal handling.
- `frontend/src/lib/entity-details.ts`: corresponding required camelCase fields.
- `frontend/src/lib/server/entity-details.ts`: parse required fields using existing timestamp/period parsers.
- `frontend/src/MemberIdentity.svelte`: append metric and update empty text.
- Existing backend summary tests and affected frontend tests: calendar boundaries, undated exclusion, exact amounts, empty state.

Rationale: the interval directly owns registration membership and avoids duplicating year-number comparisons across layers. Its start timestamp supplies the displayed year, so a separate year field cannot drift from the period. UTC and half-open boundaries handle year transitions precisely. All registered records within that year qualify, including future-dated records before the next January 1; undated declarations remain historical only. GBP, completeness, category coverage, counts, and precision continue through the existing aggregator.

